  "label": "TMUA 2019 · Paper 1 · Question 13",
  "lead": "<img class=\"source-question\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Enlarge question\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"TMUA 2019 · Paper 1 · Question 13 — Find the maximum of 4^(sin x)-4*2^(sin x)+17/4.\">",
  "options": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C",
    "D",
    "E",
    "F"
  ],
  "correct": "B",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Find the inner range",
      "body": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Since <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> and base 2 is increasing, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Optimisation after substitution must retain the exact attainable range.",
      "pitfall": "Treating u as any positive number would give a different maximum question.",
      "pause": "Rewrite <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math> as a power of u.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l07",
          "reminder": "Optimisation after substitution must retain the exact attainable range."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Complete the square",
      "body": "<p>Rewrite the full expression as a quadratic in your substituted variable. Complete its square and study it only on the interval you found.</p>",
      "recap": "For a quadratic on a restricted interval, compare the allowed vertex and endpoints.",
      "pitfall": "The completed-square constant is a minimum, while this question asks for a maximum.",
      "pause": "Find the vertex and determine which permitted endpoint is farther from it.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b2-l05",
          "reminder": "For a quadratic on a restricted interval, compare the allowed vertex and endpoints."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Choose and verify an attaining input",
      "body": "Compare the two permitted endpoint values in the completed-square expression and decide which gives the larger output. Check that the corresponding substituted value can actually be produced by the original sine expression.",
      "recap": "The input range is closed and attainable, but you must determine which endpoint gives the maximum.",
      "pitfall": "The largest substituted input need not give the largest function output.",
      "pause": "Evaluate and compare the endpoint outputs, then verify an original input attaining the larger one.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l07",
          "reminder": "A selected endpoint gives an actual extreme when the inner function reaches it."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Put <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Its full range is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>4</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. The expression is therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></math>.</p><p>For u in this interval, the distance from 2 is largest at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></math>, where it equals <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>. Thus the maximum is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo></mrow></math><strong><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>, option B.</strong></p><p>This value is attained whenever <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. At the other endpoint <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> the expression is only <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></math>, confirming that the vertex supplies the minimum instead.</p>",
